1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,620
I don't need another stock tip.

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:05,820
I need to know what changed, what I'm
missing, and whether an investment still

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:10,620
fits my plans. That's why I built Thesis,
a research companion for my own

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,990
investing decisions.

5
00:00:12,982 --> 00:00:14,262
Let's make this concrete.

6
00:00:14,282 --> 00:00:16,962
I have ten thousand dollars for a home in
two years.

7
00:00:16,982 --> 00:00:22,362
Thesis asks what I'm saving for, where I
live, and which currency I'm planning

8
00:00:22,382 --> 00:00:26,932
in. Simple choices replace a complicated
prompt.

9
00:00:28,057 --> 00:00:31,237
Next, I choose my comfort with volatility
and loss.

10
00:00:31,257 --> 00:00:33,707
A ten percent loss means a thousand
dollars.

11
00:00:35,157 --> 00:00:39,637
I also mark the deadline as firm, because
needing the money in two years

12
00:00:39,657 --> 00:00:41,107
changes what's appropriate.

13
00:00:42,075 --> 00:00:45,495
Being based in India doesn't mean
investing only in India.

14
00:00:45,515 --> 00:00:51,865
I can choose Indian investments, US
investments, or a mix, and select sectors.

15
00:00:52,715 --> 00:00:57,765
An optional equity split doesn't force my
entire budget into those markets.

16
00:00:58,865 --> 00:01:02,145
I review the amount, deadline and
preferences together.

17
00:01:02,165 --> 00:01:06,245
Explicit calculations and constraints
create the allocation.

18
00:01:06,265 --> 00:01:09,715
An optional model critique is configured
separately.

19
00:01:11,015 --> 00:01:13,495
The request becomes a saved background
job.

20
00:01:13,515 --> 00:01:17,895
I can follow its progress and return to
the result without keeping a long

21
00:01:17,915 --> 00:01:18,965
connection open.

22
00:01:19,783 --> 00:01:24,303
For this firm home deadline, Thesis
reserves the budget for accessible cash or

23
00:01:24,323 --> 00:01:26,503
a suitable deposit that matures in time.

24
00:01:26,523 --> 00:01:28,973
It doesn't force a stock allocation.

25
00:01:29,623 --> 00:01:31,703
All ten thousand dollars are accounted
for.

26
00:01:31,723 --> 00:01:36,773
The bank, rate, eligibility and currency
still need checking.

27
00:01:37,857 --> 00:01:39,637
I can also record investments.

28
00:01:39,657 --> 00:01:44,707
This illustrative entry is two Apple
shares at a price I enter myself.

29
00:01:45,357 --> 00:01:48,807
Thesis records two hundred dollars of
cost.

30
00:01:49,257 --> 00:01:54,007
Market valuation needs a separate,
entitled quote source.

31
00:01:54,457 --> 00:01:58,007
This records a holding, without placing a
broker order.

32
00:01:58,948 --> 00:02:03,328
The instrument view opens a real TradingView
chart with attribution and market

33
00:02:03,348 --> 00:02:07,128
status. The app keeps it separate from
portfolio calculations.

34
00:02:07,148 --> 00:02:12,628
An embedded chart doesn't establish
verified history for allocation or risk

35
00:02:12,648 --> 00:02:13,398
estimates.

36
00:02:14,323 --> 00:02:15,703
Now I review the evidence.

37
00:02:15,723 --> 00:02:21,173
Dated SEC facts pass through an
owner-scoped Zetaris query.

38
00:02:21,623 --> 00:02:24,673
Code identifies the available sources and
gaps.

39
00:02:25,023 --> 00:02:30,103
An NVIDIA Nemotron model, served through
Nightshift, counterchecks what those

40
00:02:30,123 --> 00:02:35,303
sources can support. Missing quotes and
price history still block market

41
00:02:35,323 --> 00:02:39,973
conclusions. Actual sources and the model
receipt stay visible.

42
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:45,957
Meterless H-MEM recalls earlier reviews so
I can revisit the reasoning.

43
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:48,787
Historical context isn't current evidence.

44
00:02:48,807 --> 00:02:55,087
News stays sourced too. Its feed was
unavailable here, and Thesis showed that

45
00:02:55,107 --> 00:02:57,457
gap instead of inventing headlines.

46
00:02:58,450 --> 00:03:04,470
Settings offer NVIDIA, OpenAI, Anthropic,
Gemini and Nightshift.

47
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:06,870
Models come from the account's actual
catalog.

48
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:10,270
Discovery and inference tests remain
separate.

49
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,540
Keys stay encrypted on the server.

50
00:03:13,090 --> 00:03:16,840
Personal providers require appropriate
keys and credits.

51
00:03:17,798 --> 00:03:21,978
Thesis brings a goal, my portfolio and the
evidence together.

52
00:03:21,998 --> 00:03:28,178
I make the decision. Next, I want
scheduled checks that flag changes in

53
00:03:28,198 --> 00:03:30,778
earnings, forecasts or legal developments.

54
00:03:30,798 --> 00:03:34,948
Today, I can start a review and inspect
what supports it.
